{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "intro",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Custom YOLOv8 Model Training for Construction Safety\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook contains the complete pipeline to train a custom YOLOv8 model for detecting construction safety objects (`person`, `helmet`, `no_helmet`, `vest`, `no_vest`, `machinery`).\n",
    "\n",
    "We are replacing the stock zero-shot YOLO-World model with a robust, fine-tuned custom model to fix the \"limb detection\" and PPE logic flaws in the original system.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Suggested Workflow:\n",
    "1. **Environment Setup:** Install `ultralytics` and `roboflow`.\n",
    "2. **Dataset:** Download an annotated Construction PPE dataset from Roboflow.\n",
    "3. **Training:** Train the YOLOv8 model for 50-100 epochs.\n",
    "4. **Export:** Export the `best.pt` file to the `ai_service/` directory."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "install",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!pip install ultralytics==8.1.0 roboflow\n",
    "import ultralytics\n",
    "ultralytics.checks()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "roboflow",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Download Dataset\n",
    "\n",
    "We will use a generic Construction PPE dataset from Roboflow. You can replace the `api_key` and project names with your own if you have a custom dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "*Note: Ensure the dataset has the explicit classes: `person`, `helmet`, `no_helmet`, `vest`, `no_vest`, `machinery`.*"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "download_data",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from roboflow import Roboflow\n",
    "\n",
    "# WARNING: Replace with your actual Roboflow API key before running in the cloud!\n",
    "# You can get one for free at app.roboflow.com\n",
    "rf = Roboflow(api_key=\"YOUR_ROBOFLOW_API_KEY_HERE\")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Example dataset (You will need to use your exact Roboflow project name here)\n",
    "project = rf.workspace(\"roboflow-universe-projects\").project(\"construction-site-safety-logs\")\n",
    "version = project.version(1)\n",
    "dataset = version.download(\"yolov8\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f\"Dataset downloaded to: {dataset.location}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "train_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Train the Model\n",
    "\n",
    "We use YOLOv8s (Small) as the base model because we need fast 15-30 FPS real-time inference on the edge/server for the React dashboard."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "train",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from ultralytics import YOLO\n",
    "\n",
    "# Load a pre-trained YOLOv8s model\n",
    "model = YOLO('yolov8s.pt')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Train the model on your dataset (Replace dataset.location with your exact path if needed)\n",
    "results = model.train(\n",
    "    data=f\"{dataset.location}/data.yaml\",  # Path to dataset yaml\n",
    "    epochs=50,                            # Number of training epochs (Increase to 100+ for better accuracy)\n",
    "    imgsze=640,                           # Image size\n",
    "    batch=16,                             # Batch size (reduce if you get Out Of Memory errors)\n",
    "    project=\"Construction_Safety\",        # Save project folder name\n",
    "    name=\"custom_yolov8s\",                # Save run name\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "export_md",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Export & Move Weights\n",
    "\n",
    "After training, your best model weights are saved in `Construction_Safety/custom_yolov8s/weights/best.pt`.\n",
    "\n",
    "We need to copy this to our `project/ai_service/` folder so `detection.py` can load it for the server."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "export",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import shutil\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "source_weights = \"Construction_Safety/custom_yolov8s/weights/best.pt\"\n",
    "target_weights = \"custom_safety_best.pt\" # Move to current dir, or directly to project/ai_service/\n",
    "\n",
    "if os.path.exists(source_weights):\n",
    "    shutil.copy(source_weights, target_weights)\n",
    "    print(f\"Success! Model weights saved to {target_weights}\")\n",
    "    print(\"You can now change YOLO_MODEL in detection.py to point to these weights.\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"Error: Training might not have finished successfully, could not find best.pt\")"
   ]
  }
